---
import ArticleLayout from '../../layouts/ArticleLayout.astro';
import { getCaseStudy } from '../../data/caseStudies';

const cs = getCaseStudy('pink-miracle');

const metaTitle = 'Pink Miracle Case Study: +110% Amazon Sales | Share It Studio';
const description =
  'How data-driven listing optimization and A/B testing took Pink Miracle, a #1-ranked shoe cleaner, from $404K to $849K in monthly Amazon sales.';

const results = [
  { metric: 'Monthly sales', before: '$404,480', after: '$606,494', change: '+51.94%', highlight: true },
  { metric: 'Units ordered', before: '20,234', after: '30,038', change: '+48.5%' },
  { metric: 'Sessions', before: '92,548', after: '121,808', change: '+31.6%' },
  { metric: 'Unit session percentage', before: '21.59%', after: '24.44%', change: '+2.85 pts' },
  { metric: 'Main image CTR (tested)', before: '2.03%', after: '2.48%', change: '+22.2%' },
];
---

<ArticleLayout
  kind="case-study"
  caseStudy={cs}
  title="How Pink Miracle grew a #1 Amazon listing to $849K in monthly sales"
  highlight="$849K in monthly sales"
  lead="Pink Miracle already ranked #1 in its category. Data-driven creative, A/B testing and weekly optimization still added +51.94% in sales in one month."
  metaTitle={metaTitle}
  description={description}
  tags={['Amazon US']}
  service={{ label: 'Amazon Listing Optimization', href: '/services/amazon-listing-optimization' }}
>
  <div class="article-body">
    <aside>
      <p>
        <strong>In short:</strong> Pink Miracle’s #1-ranked listing had outdated images and messaging. We redesigned its
        visual content, A/B tested it and optimized it every week together with the brand’s PPC manager. Monthly sales
        grew from <strong>$404,480 to $606,494 (+51.94%) in one month</strong>, and reached{' '}
        <strong>$849,312 six months later</strong>.
      </p>
    </aside>

    <section id="client-background">
      <h2>Client Background</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>Pink Miracle</strong> is an established shoe cleaner brand with a strong reputation and a top-ranking
        position on Amazon. Despite its success, the brand had significant untapped sales potential because of outdated
        listing content.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="initial-challenge">
      <h2>Initial Challenge</h2>
      <p>
        Although Pink Miracle already ranked <strong>#1 in its category</strong>, its Amazon listing lacked engaging
        visuals, clear product messaging and competitive differentiation.
      </p>
      <p>
        With approximately <strong>$404K in monthly sales</strong>, the challenge was to improve an already successful
        listing and unlock additional revenue — without disrupting its existing performance.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="our-approach">
      <h2>Our Approach</h2>
      <p>
        We developed a data-driven Amazon marketing strategy focused on improving click-through rate, conversion and
        sales through content optimization and continuous testing.
      </p>
      <p>
        The strategy combined{' '}
        <strong>PPC analysis, sales data, keyword targeting, customer-focused creative and A/B testing</strong> to find
        where the listing could improve.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="implementation">
      <h2>Implementation</h2>
      <ol class="steps-list">
        <li>
          <h3>Performance analysis</h3>
          <p>Analyzed PPC metrics, sales and customer behavior to identify optimization opportunities.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>Content optimization</h3>
          <p>
            Redesigned the main image, infographics, lifestyle images, A+ Content, Premium A+, Brand Story and videos.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>A/B testing</h3>
          <p>
            Tested main images, image stacks, product messaging and competitor comparisons with <strong>PickFu</strong>{' '}
            and <strong>Intellivy</strong>.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>Continuous optimization</h3>
          <p>Monitored CTR, CVR, sessions, units, ROAS and ACOS to guide weekly improvements.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>Performance monitoring</h3>
          <p>
            Dedicated <strong>24 hours per month</strong> to data reviews, content adjustments and coordination with the
            PPC manager.
          </p>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section id="results">
      <h2>Results</h2>
      <p>Performance one month after the new content went live, compared with the starting baseline:</p>
      <div class="table-wrap">
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th scope="col">Metric</th>
              <th scope="col">Before</th>
              <th scope="col">After</th>
              <th scope="col">Change</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            {results.map((r) => (
              <tr>
                <th scope="row">{r.metric}</th>
                <td>{r.before}</td>
                <td>{r.after}</td>
                <td class:list={{ highlight: r.highlight }}>{r.change}</td>
              </tr>
            ))}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p class="text-sm text-brand-ink/55">Main image CTR comes from a tested main image variation.</p>

      <blockquote>
        <p>
          Six months later, monthly sales reached <strong>$849,312</strong> — about <strong>110% above</strong> the
          initial baseline.
        </p>
      </blockquote>
    </section>

    <section id="key-takeaways">
      <h2>Key Takeaways</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Even top-ranking Amazon products can have significant untapped revenue potential.</li>
        <li>Data-driven creative and A/B testing help improve listing performance.</li>
        <li>Continuous monitoring and strategic content adjustments can generate measurable sales growth.</li>
        <li>High-quality visuals, supported by PPC and customer insights, strengthen conversion opportunities.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </div>
</ArticleLayout>
